IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 1: PRELIMINARY.
--
-- ss 1 (short title), 3 (purpose) and 4 (appointing the Commissioner and his
-- deputies) are not encoded as rules: NOTES.md says why, row by row.  This
-- module encodes s 2, the interpretation section, one function per defined term.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A function that can answer "not covered" returns
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the text itself gives;
-- every JUST FALSE carries a comment  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own
-- words): "..."  quoting the words.  NOTHING means the text does not answer on
-- these facts; every NOTHING carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>).  A caller must
-- never turn NOTHING into FALSE.  Definitions say "means", so a thing that is
-- not within the definition is JUST FALSE; a term the Act borrows from another
-- instrument is answered by the fact the caller states.
--
-- Each defined-term function assumes the context does not require otherwise;
-- `s 2 the definitions apply to the term as used` is the rule a caller consults
-- first.

§ `Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 -- Part 1 -- Preliminary`

§§ `s 2 Interpretation`

-- "In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires": the definitions below
-- hold unless the context requires otherwise.  Whether the context does is a
-- judgment the text leaves to the reader of the Act, so it is a plain input.
-- src:85 | Interpretation
-- src:87 | 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 (src:85-87)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the definitions apply to the term as used` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "administrator": the Board, or a public officer or public authority that the
-- Minister has appointed under s 5(4) to assist the Board.  Whether a body is a
-- public officer is a fact about its post (the Act does not define the term).
-- src:89 | “administrator” means the Board, or any public officer or public
-- src:90 | authority appointed under section 5(4) to assist the Board in
-- src:91 | administering the Scheme;
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 administrator (src:89-91)
GIVEN body IS A `Body asked about as an administrator`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the body is an administrator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body's `is the Board` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (body's `is a public officer` OR body's `is a public authority`)
           AND body's `has been appointed by the Minister under section 5(4) to assist the Board`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“administrator” means the Board, or any public officer or public authority appointed under section 5(4) to assist the Board in administering the Scheme"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "Board": the Central Provident Fund Board constituted under s 3 of the Central
-- Provident Fund Act 1953.  That Act is not among the sources, so whether a body
-- is that Board is asked as a fact; NOTHING means the caller does not know.
-- src:93 | “Board” means the Central Provident Fund Board constituted
-- src:94 | under section 3 of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953;
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 Board (src:93-94)
GIVEN `the body is the Central Provident Fund Board constituted under section 3 of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the body is the Board` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body is the Central Provident Fund Board constituted under section 3 of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)
    WHEN JUST isBoard THEN
        IF isBoard
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Board” means the Central Provident Fund Board constituted under section 3 of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "cash grant": a cash grant made by the Government under the Scheme.
-- src:96 | “cash grant” means any cash grant made by the Government
-- src:97 | under the Scheme;
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 cash grant (src:96-97)
GIVEN `the grant is made by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant is made under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the payment is a cash grant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the grant is made by the Government` AND `the grant is made under the Scheme` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cash grant” means any cash grant made by the Government under the Scheme"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "Commissioner": the Commissioner for Silver Support appointed under s 4(1)
-- and any Deputy or Assistant Commissioner appointed under s 4(2).  The
-- appointment itself is the Minister's act (s 4, machinery); here it is a fact.
-- src:99 | “Commissioner” means the Commissioner for Silver Support
-- src:100 | appointed under section 4(1), and includes any Deputy
-- src:101 | Commissioner for Silver Support or Assistant Commissioner
-- src:102 | for Silver Support appointed under section 4(2);
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 Commissioner (src:99-102)
GIVEN appointment IS AN `Appointment under section 4`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the person is the Commissioner` MEANS
    CONSIDER appointment
    WHEN `appointed under section 4(1) as the Commissioner for Silver Support` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `appointed under section 4(2)(a) as a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `appointed under section 4(2)(b) as an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Commissioner” means the Commissioner for Silver Support appointed under section 4(1), and includes any Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support or Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support appointed under section 4(2)"
    WHEN `not appointed under section 4` THEN JUST FALSE

-- "eligible individual": "an individual who is eligible to receive any benefit
-- under the Scheme".  This is the second statement of the same status; s 6(1)
-- states the conditions and s 7(1) the entitlement.  FORK F-1 in NOTES.md: the
-- two statements are read as one status, so this function takes the answer of
-- s 6(1) and s 7(1) (the caller passes it) and does not decide it a second time.
-- src:104 | “eligible individual” means an individual who is eligible to
-- src:105 | receive any benefit under the Scheme;
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 eligible individual (src:104-105)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is eligible to receive any benefit under the Scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the person is an eligible individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“eligible individual” means an individual who is eligible to receive any benefit under the Scheme"
        IF NOT `the person is an individual` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“eligible individual” means an individual who is eligible to receive any benefit under the Scheme"
        IF `the individual is eligible to receive any benefit under the Scheme` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what benefits are prescribed, and for whom, is for regulations
        IF `the individual is eligible to receive any benefit under the Scheme` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "investigator": an officer or employee of the Board authorised under s 5(7),
-- and any person the Minister appointed under s 5(8) to assist.
-- src:107 | “investigator” means an officer or employee of the Board who is
-- src:108 | authorised under section 5(7) to conduct any investigation
-- src:109 | under this Act, and includes any person appointed under
-- src:110 | section 5(8) to assist the Board in conducting any
-- src:111 | investigation under this Act;
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 investigator (src:107-111)
GIVEN person IS A `Person asked about as an investigator`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the person is an investigator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF person's `is an officer or employee of the Board authorised under section 5(7) to conduct an investigation under this Act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person's `has been appointed under section 5(8) to assist the Board in conducting an investigation under this Act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“investigator” means an officer or employee of the Board who is authorised under section 5(7) to conduct any investigation under this Act, and includes any person appointed under section 5(8) to assist the Board in conducting any investigation under this Act"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "means information": information about the income or assets of an individual
-- or of the individuals who make up a household, held by a Government
-- department or public authority.
-- src:116 | “means information” means any information relating to the
-- src:117 | income or assets of any individual, or of a group of
-- src:118 | individuals who comprise a household, in the possession of
-- src:119 | any Government department or public authority;
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 means information (src:116-119)
GIVEN information IS AN `Information asked about as means information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the information is means information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (information's `relates to the income or assets of an individual`
            OR information's `relates to the income or assets of a group of individuals who comprise a household`)
           AND information's `is in the possession of a Government department or public authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“means information” means any information relating to the income or assets of any individual, or of a group of individuals who comprise a household, in the possession of any Government department or public authority"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "permanent resident of Singapore": "has the meaning given by section 2 of the
-- Immigration Act 1959".  That Act is not among the sources, so the meaning is
-- the caller's fact; this function passes the stated fact on and does not decide
-- it.  (Amended by Act 31 of 2023 wef 1 December 2025: the in-force text.)
-- src:121 | “permanent resident of Singapore” has the meaning given by
-- src:122 | section 2 of the Immigration Act 1959;
-- src:124 | [Act 31 of 2023 wef 01/12/2025]
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 permanent resident of Singapore (src:121-124)
GIVEN `the person is a permanent resident within the meaning given by section 2 of the Immigration Act 1959` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the person is a permanent resident of Singapore` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is a permanent resident within the meaning given by section 2 of the Immigration Act 1959`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- the answer is the stated fact, passed on: the meaning is given by another Act
    WHEN JUST stated THEN JUST stated

-- "public authority": a body established or constituted by or under a public Act
-- to perform or discharge a public function.
-- src:126 | “public authority” means a body established or constituted by or
-- src:127 | under a public Act to perform or discharge a public function;
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 public authority (src:126-127)
GIVEN body IS A `Body asked about as a public authority`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the body is a public authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body's `is a body established or constituted by or under a public Act`
           AND body's `is to perform or discharge a public function`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public authority” means a body established or constituted by or under a public Act to perform or discharge a public function"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "public scheme": (a) established by or under written law and administered by
-- a public authority or by the Government in another manner; and (b) to provide
-- financial relief, assistance or support to citizens of Singapore or permanent
-- residents of Singapore, or any part of them.  (Amended by Act 31 of 2023 wef
-- 31 December 2024: the in-force text.)
-- src:129 | “public scheme” means any scheme that —
-- src:131 | (a) is or will be established by or under any written law
-- src:132 | and administered by a public authority, or by the
-- src:133 | Government in any other manner; and
-- src:135 | (b) is to provide financial relief, assistance or support to
-- src:136 | citizens of Singapore or permanent residents of
-- src:137 | Singapore, or any part of them;
-- src:139 | [Act 31 of 2023 wef 31/12/2024]
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 public scheme (src:129-139)
GIVEN scheme IS A `Scheme asked about as a public scheme`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the scheme is a public scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (    scheme's `is or will be established by or under written law`
            AND (   scheme's `is or will be administered by a public authority`
                 OR scheme's `is or will be administered by the Government in any other manner`))
           AND (   scheme's `is to provide financial relief, assistance or support to citizens of Singapore`
                OR scheme's `is to provide financial relief, assistance or support to permanent residents of Singapore`
                OR scheme's `is to provide financial relief, assistance or support to a part of those citizens or permanent residents`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public scheme” means any scheme that"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "Scheme": the Silver Support Scheme established under s 5(1).
-- src:141 | “Scheme” means the Silver Support Scheme established under
-- src:142 | section 5(1).
@ref SSSA2015 s 2 Scheme (src:141-142)
GIVEN `the scheme is the Silver Support Scheme established under section 5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the scheme is the Scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the scheme is the Silver Support Scheme established under section 5(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Scheme” means the Silver Support Scheme established under section 5(1)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
